.TH VAULT-CP 1 "September 2026" "vault" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vault-cp \- copy a stored file or folder
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vault cp
.RB [ \-r ]
.RB [ \-\-key
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-vault
.IR DIR ]
.I OLD NEW
.SH DESCRIPTION
Copies \fIOLD\fR to \fINEW\fR, following the same naming rules as
.BR vault\-mv (1).
A folder needs \fB\-r\fR. The copy shares the original's encrypted
objects rather than re-encrypting them, so it is instant and takes no
extra space; deleting either name leaves the other intact.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-r
Copy a folder and everything under it.
.TP
.BI \-\-key " PATH"
Key file. Default: $VAULT_KEY, else ~/.vault/key.
.TP
.BI \-\-vault " DIR"
Vault directory. Default: $VAULT_DIR, else ~/.vault/store.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VAULT_PASSPHRASE
Passphrase, instead of prompting on the terminal.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vault (1),
.BR vault\-mv (1),
.BR vault\-rm (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andy Dixon <vault@dixon.cx>, https://www.dixon.cx
